keywords:
  - "natural language processing"
  - "large language models"
  - "semantic protocol"
  - "AI-to-AI communication"
  - "AI Act compliance"
  - "deontic logic"
  - "multi-agent systems"
  - "compression"
abstract: >
  CSTL (Compressed Semantic Transfer Language) is a textual semantic
  protocol designed for lossless LLM-to-LLM communication. It preserves
  propositional content, deontic modalities ([MUST], [NOT], [IF]),
  numerical force, temporality, uncertainty markers, and multi-agent
  trust state across agent hops. CSTL is self-sufficient (no shared
  infrastructure required), zero-shot intelligible by frontier LLMs
  (Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT), and aligned with EU AI Act articles
  12, 13, and 14 for record-keeping, transparency, and human oversight.
  Empirical validation across 9 distinct test protocols achieves
  212/214 = 99.1% factual fidelity preservation.
